---
alwaysApply: true
---

* Use `uv` to manage packages
* Remember that the project is primarily aimed at running on a raspberry pi under raspberry pi OS
* Run the tests when you make changes
* Always use todo lists to keep track of what you need to do
* Use `ssh pi@raspberrypi.local` to connect and run commands on the raspberry pi. On the pi:
    - `uv` is setup
    - to get files onto the pi, you can commit & push your changes and then pull them on the raspberry pi (make sure you're both on the same branch!)
    - do not mess with origin's git history! (non destructive operations only to the git remote)
    - alex-assistant (this repo) is already git cloned into /home/pi/alex-assistant
